# The Dockerfiles (tempogate, and the e2e mock-Google and cliclient images)
# all build from the repo root and need only the Go module: sources, go:embed
# assets (oidc/templates, state/sqlite/migrations) and test/e2e/cliclient's
# xdg-open shim. Leaving the rest out keeps the context small and lets
# docs- or chart-only changes reuse the cached `COPY . .` layer.
#
# .git is not needed: version info comes from build args, and the builder
# image has no git, so Go never stamped VCS info into the binary anyway.
.git
.github
.claude
.bin
dist
coverage.*
*.db
.env
Casks
charts
docs
examples
**/*.md
